x11: fix integrated title bar double-click to maximize

The first press starts a WM drag; the WM grabs the keyboard for it,
sending FocusOut/FocusIn with mode Grab/Ungrab. We treat that as focus
loss and clear last_mouse_click, so the second press is never streak 2.

Ignore focus events with mode Grab/Ungrab, like GLFW does:
https://github.com/glfw/glfw/blob/92dcf4ce74f2e2554a98fea09be7c705c17daa5a/src/x11_window.c#L1745-L1751

Needs 02-drag.patch, else the second press is swallowed.

Tested on muffin (Cinnamon).

diff --git a/window/src/os/x11/window.rs b/window/src/os/x11/window.rs
index 8bc6f62..b0b7bb3 100644
--- a/window/src/os/x11/window.rs
+++ b/window/src/os/x11/window.rs
@@ -844,13 +844,25 @@ impl XWindowInner {
                     self.verify_focus = true;
                 }
             }
+            // Grab/Ungrab focus events come from a keyboard grab, e.g. the
+            // WM grabbing during a window drag; focus hasn't really moved.
             Event::X(xcb::x::Event::FocusIn(e)) => {
-                if !matches!(e.detail(), xcb::x::NotifyDetail::Pointer) {
+                if !matches!(e.detail(), xcb::x::NotifyDetail::Pointer)
+                    && !matches!(
+                        e.mode(),
+                        xcb::x::NotifyMode::Grab | xcb::x::NotifyMode::Ungrab
+                    )
+                {
                     self.focus_changed(true);
                 }
             }
             Event::X(xcb::x::Event::FocusOut(e)) => {
-                if !matches!(e.detail(), xcb::x::NotifyDetail::Pointer) {
+                if !matches!(e.detail(), xcb::x::NotifyDetail::Pointer)
+                    && !matches!(
+                        e.mode(),
+                        xcb::x::NotifyMode::Grab | xcb::x::NotifyMode::Ungrab
+                    )
+                {
                     self.focus_changed(false);
                 }
             }
